Z||000000||KnightRyder31||04-30-2000||09:00 PM||||My Buddy and I when to look at this sweet looking 86 Fiero SE V6 with 96,000 miles. Its red, and the paint was in great cond. He said that it needed the arm for one of the lights, and the exhaust was leeking a bit. I also noticed a little oil leek, and it had a cracked windshield. Besides that the car was in great cond. I test drove it, and it drives real nice. It has rear defrost, and electric decklid switches. The guy is asking $1,800 for it. I dont think its too bad of a price. Do you guys think its worth that much considering what I told you about the car?<BR>----Knight----||||reg||4
Z||000001||kornholio||04-30-2000||09:59 PM||||Hey KnightRyder31,<BR>I can't help but plug my 2m6 that's for sale... <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum4/HTML/000687.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum4/HTML/000687.html</A> <P>I noticed in your profile that you are from Waterford MI.  Is that near to Port Huron MI?  I'm in London, Ontario which is about an hour away from Port Huron.||||reg||1
Z||000002||KnightRyder31||04-30-2000||10:50 PM||||Ok, off the bat, is there anything wrong with the car? How fast have you had it going? Tell me a little more about your car.<BR>Have you had any mods done to it?<BR>-----Knight------||||reg||1
Z||000003||batboy||04-30-2000||11:28 PM||||The car has a cracked windshield, probably a cracked exhaust manifold (could be a hole in the muffler, but expect the worse), the headlights, or at least one, don't work (I don't know what a light arm is, but the gears could be stripped or a bad relay, etc.--can be a hassle), and you have an oil leak that could be a valve cover gasket or a rear main or anything in between (rear main requires dropping the entire engine and tranny, lots of work). Sounds like a lot of money and/or time to repair. Also sound like this guy didn't keep up with the maintenance. If you really want it offer a lot less, maybe $1000, or ask if he'll have all that fixed for the price (of course he won't, that's why he's getting rid of it, it'll cost too much to repair).||||reg||1
Z||000004||KnightRyder31||05-01-2000||03:10 PM||||Tell me, how much $ in repairs?<BR>----Knight----||||reg||1
Z||000005||kornholio||05-01-2000||06:54 PM||||There's nothing wrong with my car.  It is and will still remain my daily driver until I sell it.  It needs nothing to be certified.  I am selling it because I need more trunk space and passenger room.  The only mods I have done to this car are the "toys" (CD player, remote start, fog lights, alarm/keyless entry).  The fastest I have been in this car is only 140 km/h.  That's because I'm afraid of the consequences...my friend got caught doing 170 km/h in a 100 km/h speed limit.  That's a trip to court for that fool!||||reg||1
Z||000006||KnightRyder31||05-01-2000||10:33 PM||||I already have a Fiero. I just want a V6, my current one has only the L4. Its a 84' Fiero coupe with only 64,500 miles on it. I baby the car. Its white in color. Has the rear defrost. I payed $2,300 for it, its is near mint. If I can sell my car for $2,500 I would buy yours....I really need a V6!<BR>----Knight----||||reg||1
